# Hit effects and missiles swapped from Lua (pair 29 condition auras, element blasts, hit splashes and missiles;
# server/README.md "Condition auras, blasts and fireworks (pair 29)"). The engine draws the hit effect of every damage
# part itself (Game::combatGetTypeInfo: a red splash on a blood creature, small stock sparks for an element, the same
# for each tick of a burning or poison condition) and every missile by its stock id. Now Lua may swap them:
#   Game.setHitEffect(kind, key, effect[, dx, dy])  kind 0: a physical hit on a creature of race `key`; 1: a direct
#       hit of combat type `key`; 2: a condition tick of combat type `key`. The effect is sent at the target tile +
#       (dx, dy) (an effect bigger than a tile is drawn up-left of its tile); 0 sends none; nil or -1 gives the stock
#       one back. The splash item and the text colour stay the engine's.
#   Game.setMissileEffect(stock, missile[, dx, dy])  every distance effect `stock` (spells, runes, wands, monsters,
#       Lua sendDistanceEffect) is sent as `missile`, both ends shifted by (dx, dy); missile 0 or nil: stock again.
#   Game.clearEffectOverrides()  all stock again.
# Nothing is set by default: without a Lua call every effect is the stock one. data/lib/chaos_pack29_vfx.lua sets
# them at startup only when the pair 29 switch is on (ChaosPack29Fx.PAIR29), and only for effect ids that pair has.
# Guard: server/tools/effect_overrides_patch_test.py. Applies after 0001-0044.
